  "prompt_text": "This figure is a simplified structural diagram of a coronavirus particle, showing how its main components are arranged within and on the viral envelope. The virus is drawn as a roughly spherical, membrane-bound particle. Projecting from the outer surface are large spike proteins, which form the distinctive crown-like appearance, along with smaller membrane proteins and a few envelope proteins embedded in the lipid boundary.\n\nInside the particle, a long strand of RNA is shown coiled through the interior and associated with nucleocapsid protein, indicating that the viral genome is packaged as a ribonucleoprotein complex rather than existing freely. The image emphasizes that the coronavirus is an enveloped RNA virus whose infectivity and structure depend on several coordinated protein classes: spikes on the outside, structural membrane components in the envelope, and genome-binding nucleocapsid inside.\n\nOverall, the figure conveys the basic architecture of the virus rather than a dynamic process. Its main message is the spatial organization of key coronavirus structural elements and how the genome is enclosed within a protein-lined membrane carrying multiple surface proteins involved in viral structure and host interaction.",
